docs/DEVELOPMENT.md --- 2/2 --- Text
22 22 Run `just check` for the full local gate and `just e2e` for browser acceptance. Portable CI uses `bash scripts/ci.sh` after fetching locked dependencies. Commands have timeouts; HEAVENKEY_DEADLINE_UTC can impose a shared cutoff. The original eight-hour spike budget remains historical evidence.
23 23 
24 24 CI uses read-only permission, pinned action commit SHAs and a 20-minute job limit. It runs on push, pull_request and manual dispatch, with no deployment or real authenticator. The design follows [GitHub secure-use guidance](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use).
   25 
   26 The user explicitly authorized v0.3 expert subagents. Three lanes own Rust credential lifecycle, browser UI/E2E and donor research/security review. The controller owns image, documentation, package pins, integration and acceptance. Writers have disjoint files and no commit authority; only one fixed-port E2E runs at a time. No acceleration multiplier or financial saving is inferred from parallel work.

